The way I see it, for a Caveman the sling is a better ranged weapon
than a bow.  nethack.wikia.com is pretty dismissive of the sling, even
for Cavemen, and I don=92t really understand why.  Here is how I see the
advantages and disadvantages for the sling for Cavemen:

Advantages:
d6 is on par with normal arrows.  Ya and elven arrows do 0.5 damage
more, but are not as easy to get as normal arrows are from arrow
traps.
Cavemen can fire d3 flint stones at maximum skill and only d2 arrows.
Flint stones don=92t break, so the initial inventory should last the
whole game.

Disadvantages:
No silver sling ammo.  (I wonder though whether you can sling silver
rings?).
Flint stones are 10x heavier than arrows.

The lack of silver damage is mitigated for a Caveman by the fact that
the Sceptre of Might does double damage against non-lawfuls.  As for
the weight, this is the same as dagger weight and no one disses
DaggerStorm even though they do less damage per projectile than flint
stones.

What am I missing?

